From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: retain PCI LTSSM startup workaround

Retain the existing downstream workaround for startup crashes on BPI-Rx
boards. The original patch reported incorrect register addresses on those
PCI controllers and carried no author metadata.

The early return bypasses LTSSM setup for every device using this PCI
reset path. It is not restricted to BPI boards and requires platform
validation before it can be narrowed or removed. This patch header update
keeps the previously compiled driver code unchanged.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -249,6 +249,9 @@ static void ath12k_pci_enable_ltssm(stru
 	u32 val;
 	int i;
 
+	/* Prevent startup crash on BPI-Rx */
+	return;
+
 	val = ath12k_pci_read32(ab, PCIE_PCIE_PARF_LTSSM);
 
 	/* PCIE link seems very unstable after the Hot Reset*/
